			"Message": "style(Worker): Revert ESBuild configurations to readable PascalCase format\n\nThe ESBuild configuration files in `Configuration/ESBuild/` were inadvertently minified, compressing variable names to single letters (e.g., `i`, `o`, `t`, `e`, `r`, `n`) and collapsing control flow into dense blocks. This contradicts the project's strict PascalCase naming convention for all variables and functions, even in build scripts, and severely hampers readability and maintainability.\n\nRevert `Target.js` and `Configuration/ESBuild/Worker.js` to the expanded, readable format used in the source `Source/Configuration/ESBuild/Worker.js`. Ensure all local variables and exports follow PascalCase (e.g., `On`, `Clean`, `Default`). Restore descriptive destructuring and explicit control flow statements. The source configuration remains the source of truth, ensuring consistency across the Worker element's build pipeline without altering the underlying build logic or output behavior.",
